    "tactics": "Ghouls use stealth and climbing to ambush prey from unexpected angles. They use Multiattack to maximize chances of landing paralytic claw strikes, then feast on paralyzed victims. They gang up on dangerous foes to trigger multiple paralysis saves.",
    "attacksNotes": "<p>Bite [Combat]: Melee attack (Agil 7 + Melee Combat 5), Reach: 5 ft</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Margin 1:</strong>: 10 damage (6 + 4 Str)</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 2:</strong> 10 damage, DR halved (round up)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Claws [Combat]: Melee attack (Agil 7 + Melee Combat 5), Reach: 5 ft</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Margin 1:</strong>: 8 damage (4 + 4 Str)</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 2:</strong> 8 damage, DR halved (round up)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Special: On hit target must make Fortitude [Easy] save or become Paralyzed for 1 minute. Paralyzed creatures can repeat save at end of each turn (2 successes ends early, 1 success adds Fortune to next save)</p>",
    "specialAbilitiesNotes": "<p>Paralytic Claws: Creatures hit by claw ### Attacks must save vs paralysis (see Claws attack). Spider Climb: Can climb difficult surfaces including upside-down on ceilings without ability checks. Paralyze Immunity: Ghouls and other undead are immune to ghoul paralysis.</p>",
